From 064247ea3a174bbbc20d7cd35d8dd4e6dfa4f975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:29:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Bluetooth: hci_conn: don't reuse an aborting SCO
 connection

hci_connect_sco() finds an existing connection to the destination by
type and address only, and sets up a link only if that connection is
BT_OPEN or BT_CLOSED. A connection that is being disconnected is
neither: hci_abort_conn() only sets abort_reason, and the connection
stays BT_CONNECTED until the Disconnection Complete event arrives.

A socket that connects to the same device in that window is therefore
handed the dying connection. No Setup Synchronous Connection is sent,
sco_connect() reports the socket connected at once, and the
Disconnection Complete then closes it with ECONNABORTED. Closing a SCO
socket and connecting a new one right away, as PipeWire does when the
HFP codec changes during a call, ends with a socket that reported
success and never had a link.

Fail the connect with -ECONNABORTED when the connection found has
abort_reason set, and drop the ACL reference hci_connect_acl() took.
The caller learns at once, with the error the socket would otherwise
get later, and can connect again once the link is gone.

Fixes: a13f316e90fd ("Bluetooth: hci_conn: Consolidate code for aborting connections")
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
index 29da3fe2b9538..8a20ccdf618c7 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
@@ -1909,6 +1909,14 @@ struct hci_conn *hci_connect_sco(struct hci_dev *hdev, int type, bdaddr_t *dst,
 			hci_conn_drop(acl);
 			return sco;
 		}
+	} else if (sco->abort_reason) {
+		/* The connection is being disconnected and stays BT_CONNECTED
+		 * until the Disconnection Complete event, so no setup would
+		 * be sent for it and it would be closed under the new socket
+		 * as soon as the event arrives.
+		 */
+		hci_conn_drop(acl);
+		return ERR_PTR(-ECONNABORTED);
 	}
 
 	link = hci_conn_link(acl, sco);

